<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C5.S1 — Depolarizing noise on the Bloch ball</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C5.S1 — Contraction of the Bloch vector</p></div><p>The depolarizing channel acts as \(\mathcal D_p(\rho)=(1-p)\rho+p\,\frac{I}{2}\).</p><p>(a) Starting from \(|0\rangle\), give \(\langle Z\rangle\) after the channel, as a function of <code>p</code>.</p><p>\(\langle Z\rangle=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) Give the purity \(\operatorname{tr}\rho^{2}\) of the output, as a function of <code>p</code>.</p><p>purity \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In Bloch form \(\rho=\tfrac12(I+\vec r\cdot\vec\sigma)\) and \(\mathcal D_p:\vec r\mapsto(1-p)\vec r\): the ball shrinks uniformly toward its centre.</p><p>(a) \(|0\rangle\) has \(\vec r=(0,0,1)\), so \(\langle Z\rangle=1-p\).</p><p>(b) \(\operatorname{tr}\rho^2=\tfrac12(1+\|\vec r\|^2)=\tfrac12(1+(1-p)^2)\).</p><p>At \(p=1\) the output is \(I/2\): all information is destroyed and the purity is \(1/2\), the minimum for a qubit. Note \(p=1\) is <em>not</em> the worst case for error correction — a fully depolarizing channel is at least known, whereas intermediate \(p\) leaves partial, correctable information.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1000000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
