  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>C5.S3 — Amplitude damping and the T1 model</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:16px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;"><p style="color:#026573;font-family:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0;">C5.S3 — Energy relaxation</p></div><p>Amplitude damping has Kraus operators \(K_0=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&\sqrt{1-\gamma}\end{pmatrix}\), \(K_1=\begin{pmatrix}0&\sqrt\gamma\\0&0\end{pmatrix}\).</p><p>(a) Starting from \(|1\rangle\), give the probability of finding the qubit in \(|0\rangle\) after the channel.</p><p>\(p_0=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p><p>(b) If the channel is applied \(n\) times in succession, give the probability of still finding \(|1\rangle\).</p><p>\(p_1^{(n)}=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p><p>(c) Writing \(\gamma=1-e^{-t/T_1}\) for a single application of duration \(t\), give \(p_1\) as a function of <code>t</code> and <code>T1</code>.</p><p>\(p_1(t)=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(K_1|1\rangle=\sqrt\gamma\,|0\rangle\), so \(p_0=\gamma\).</p><p>(b) Each application leaves \(|1\rangle\) with probability \(1-\gamma\), and the \(|1\rangle\) component is not repopulated, so \(p_1^{(n)}=(1-\gamma)^n\).</p><p>(c) With \(\gamma=1-e^{-t/T_1}\), \(p_1=e^{-t/T_1}\) — the exponential energy relaxation measured on real hardware as \(T_1\). Dephasing gives the complementary \(T_2\) timescale, with \(T_2\le 2T_1\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
